From 644a84e4ec611236a8056172ae10fcf45f57b1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uzair Aftab <git@uzaaft.me>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:41:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] kk: wire poly geometry shader emulation (geometryShader
 feature)

Port honeykrisp's poly-based GS wiring: poly_nir_lower_gs produces the
main/count/pre-GS compute variants plus a synthesized rasterization
vertex shader; the compute prepasses dispatch before the render draw
(sw-VS then main GS) and the draw is rewritten to source the emulation
output (static/dynamic indexed shapes from the poly heap, 8-bit static
topologies widened to 16-bit for Metal).

Notes vs honeykrisp:
- Variants are packed into extra MSL slots on the vertex shader object
  (KK_MSL_SLOT_GS_*) mirroring KK's tessellation packing.
- poly grids are thread counts but Metal indirect dispatch has
  threadgroup granularity, so the compute variants get an x-dimension
  bounds guard against the grid in the param structs.
- Transform feedback and pipeline-statistics queries are not wired yet:
  the count/pre-GS variants are compiled but not dispatched, and
  load_stat_query_address_poly lowers to null.
- tess+GS combined pipelines are not supported yet (TES would need to
  compile as a software vertex shader feeding the GS prepass).

Verified: Vulkan GS render test (point amplified to fullscreen triangle
via VS+GS+FS, offscreen render + readback, all pixels correct) on
Apple M3 Max.
